---
import { t, changeLanguage } from "i18next";
import { localizePath } from "astro-i18next";
import { Trans } from "astro-i18next/components";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/BlogPost.astro";

changeLanguage("es");
---

<Layout
	title={t("nixon.title")}
	heroImage="../../../images/data/nv_dark.png"
	description={t("nixon.desc")}
>
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.intro">
		<p>
			THE NIXONVERSE is a tale developed by MISTER MANTICORE (Alex
			Casanas) via YouTube. The series is a Spin-Off of his main story,
			<a href={localizePath("/monument_mythos")}>THE MONUMENT MYTHOS</a>.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.synop">
		<h1>SYNOPSIS</h1>
		<p>
			The series take place after the events of the second season of
			MONUMENT MYTHOS, in a different universe with a familiar form; the
			story connects four entities very similar and powerful: the Son, the
			Knight, the Queen and... <i>God</i>. With these entities, there are
			some eyes that glow more than others, those being from Alice Avenue,
			Ed Dwight, and the egocentric self of the United States, always
			obsessed with power.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<h1>{t("chrono.chrono")}</h1>
		<h1>CHRONOLOGY</h1>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/VdcCQmMEKtk" target="_blank">THE LAST SON OF ALCATRAZ</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/p18oxjNauM8" target="_blank"> THE D-DAY KNIGHT</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/oWyklL0biuo" target="_blank">THE QUEEN OF THE LUNARIANS</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/DLWmWR8HrdI" target="_blank">JESUS IN VIETNAM</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/vyxYFnxd7Q8" target="_blank">THE MISSING EYE OF JESUS CHRIST</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/D86OD5fa_aY" target="_blank">THE HOUSE IN THE OCEAN</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/IeRZ8USiRKI" target="_blank"> SEA OF THE LAST SON</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/gsXYUfw_09I" target="_blank">THE D-DAY KNIGHT RETURNS</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/zsZwjmOe2pc" target="_blank"> D-DAY KNIGHTFALL</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/nYKzDV8T58A" target="_blank"> NIXON IS GOD</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://youtu.be/Nmi3ENEOMXQ" target="_blank">THE ED DWIGHT PARADOX</a>
			</li>
		</ol>

	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part1">
		<h1>INTERPRETATION</h1>
		<center>
			<p>
				<b>
					Faster than an airplane! More powerful than a locomotive!
					Impervious to bullets! Up in the sky, look! It's a bird!
					It's a plane! It's--
				</b>
			</p>
		</center>
		<p>
			Our story begins with <strong>The Last Son</strong>, a real
			superhero who is always there to save us all, and yet some people
			are in constant fear that he will rebel against us and conquer us.
			It's worth noting that his physical appearance resembles Richard
			Nixon too closely when he was young.
		</p>
		<p>
			Actually, he is not our only hero, there is another one baptized
			<strong>The D-Day Knight</strong>, the one who saved the US Army on
			the battlefield that day in 1944. He gave us all hope and faith from
			his intervention in Normandy, and no one more than Alice Avenue had
			great respect and affection for him. During D-Day, the Knight lost
			something that will prove very interesting later on, he lost his
			helmet.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img src="../../../images/data/hornedhelmet_dark.png" class="logo toggleable" />
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part2">
		<blockquote>
			<center><p><i> D-Day Knight's Helmet</i></p></center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			That's the beginning of our planet, but what if we go up? Somewhere
			like... <i>the Moon.</i>
		</p>
		<p>
			The first mission to land humans on the Moon was not as normal as
			you might think, because Ed Dwight (the first man on the Moon) and
			his team found the <strong>Queen of the Lunarians</strong>, and
			witnessed the first recorded words on our natural satellite. The
			queen prophesied a Great Division on Earth, since humans did not
			know how to live, how to love, how to fly... Unfortunately, a small
			bloodstain covered the moment, because after ordering Ed to shoot
			her, John Glenn was <b>evicted from reality</b>.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img src="../../../images/data/johndeath_dark.png" class="logo toggleable" />
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part3">
		<blockquote>
			<center>
				<p>
					<i> John Glenn's cause of death: a Lunarian encounter.</i>
				</p>
			</center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			It's at this very moment that Ed Dwight would have a very
			interesting talk with <i>someone special,</i> but we'll come back to
			that later. Now that we know our protagonists, we can move on to our
			antagonist: United States.
		</p>
		<center>
			<p>
				After interfering in the Korean War, THE LAST SON returned to
				his fortress in Alaska. <b
					>Nuclear missiles followed him home.</b
				>
			</p>
		</center>
		<p>
			After the Apollo 11 mission revealed the properties of the Lunarian
			anatomy, the United States wasted no time in sending Apollo 12 to
			bring back the perfect ingredient to fulfil the devious plan: a
			Lunarian Eye. Phase one was completed, but something was still
			missing... or rather, somebody. An eye of an alien race and the
			equivalent of Superman, why would the proclaimed land of freedom
			want these elements? Easy, <b>to create their own Jesus</b>.
		</p>
		<p>
			After brainwashing the Last Son, the United States would bring a
			distorted version of peace during the Vietnam War, now called
			Bethlenam or “The First Saved State”; this fake treaty was referred
			to as The Peace Equation.
		</p>
		<blockquote>
			<center>
				<p>
					<i
						>OUR FREEDOM ᐳ YOUR FREEDOM
						<br />OUR CHRIST ᐳ YOUR CHRIST
						<br />= WORLD PEACE</i
					>
				</p>
			</center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			In a turn of events, the Last Son opened his eyes (well... his one
			eye), and realized all the horrifying acts he had committed under
			the mantle of the Messiah. Devastated by this, he fled to the ocean
			of his former home, Dark Alaska, and sought a refuge isolated from
			man, something that would remind him of his childhood, something
			like... a <a href={localizePath("/house_in_the_ocean")}
				>House in the Ocean</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Fate is very funny, because some time later the Last Son would have
			an encounter with a ship of a race we know very well, the Lunarians
			come to fulfil a prophecy: bring their King back home. <strong>
				The Crescent King was born.</strong
			>
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img src="../../../images/data/evolution_dark.png" class="logo toggleable" />
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part4">
		<blockquote>
			<center><p><i>Evolution ofthe Last Son.</i></p></center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			Slowly, the Lunarians began to take control of America, not only by
			creating “vessels for the king's essence”, but also by attacking the
			human culture, starting with language. No one understood their own
			thoughts, so they had to accept the Lunarian culture by force in
			order to survive. However, in the midst of all this storm, a
			familiar voice returned to bring faith to the human race... Alice
			Avenue broadcasted over the radio the story of the Last Son.
		</p>
		<p>
			The Last Son was a young man like you and me, with parents who were
			cutthroats and classmates who were worse. The boy was always alone
			when he went to school, and always in those moments driving towards
			his destiny, he doubted his role in the universe; he always thought
			that he had to help everyone around him, and that he had to win at
			any cost. One day in the midst of his thoughts, the young man was
			involved in a car crash; still strong enough to move, he got out of
			his car and approached the dying man with whom he had collided, a
			familiar face from another universe... <b>James Dean</b>.
		</p>
		<p>
			“You won, little bastard... you won...”, this were the last words of
			the man who in this universe, lost. The Last Son was devastated and
			could not hold back his tears, and from the pain and exhaustion
			caused by the accident, he fainted. He woke up in a strange dream,
			where he found himself on a cliff with a vehicle behind him, which
			was driving at high speed. He, to avoid the impact, jumped into the
			void, and began to believe more and more that he could fly, that he
			could beat death... he did it. The young man began to fly high,
			faster than an airplane. It was right here that he woke up and flew
			as far away as possible from the scene of the accident. He kept on
			believing, and kept on winning at any cost in order to save
			everyone.
		</p>
		<p>
			Alice not only prayed that the Crescent King would remember the hero
			he was before America captured him, she also hoped that the Knight
			would return to save us all again. He listened to her words and
			executed a desperate plan to make the humanity of the Last Son wake
			up again: throw Alice off the top of the Chrysler Building hoping
			that he would rescue her... <b>that never happened</b>.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img src="../../../images/data/avenuefall_dark.png" class="logo toggleable" />
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part5">
		<blockquote>
			<center><p><i>Alice Avenue's last moments of life.</i></p></center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			After the Knight's plan failed in every way, the Lunarians continued
			their invasion, brainwashing and altering human brains in major
			cities such as New York. It's at this point that the Knight would
			compose a message apologizing for what happened to Alice, and that
			she was still alive...
		</p>
		<center
			><p>
				<a href={localizePath("/monument_mythos")}
					>IN MY WORLD, STATUES HELD SOULS</a
				>
			</p></center
		>
		<p>
			Something still left the Knight unsatisfied, something made him feel
			hollow, so to try to redeem himself he removed the head of the Alice
			Avenue memorial statue and wear it as if it were his old helmet;
			even though he had only worn it for a day something in him changed,
			the only thing that could be seen was his eye, full of anger... <b
				><i>Grief can make you a monster</i></b
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			This precise moment is where Apollo 11 comes back to play a vital
			role, so we'll have to go back in time a bit, and put ourselves in
			Ed Dwight's spacesuit again. His body was found on the moon, and it
			was determined that his death was caused by his own weapon; next to
			him was a tape which would be referred to as “THE MOON GOD”. On this
			tape is revealed the conversation Ed had with that someone special
			who has been hidden for quite some time, the God behind the beings
			that are causing so much damage right now... <b>Richard Nixon</b>.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img src="../../../images/data/god_dark.png" class="logo toggleable" />
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part6">
		<blockquote>
			<center><p><i>Photograph of God<br />By Ed Dwight</i></p></center>
		</blockquote>
		<center
			><h5>
				Note: The following audio does not feature the voice of Ed
				Dwight.
			</h5></center
		>
		<p>
			Nixon explains in this tape that he managed to escape from the
			Horned Serpent during the Great Division, and that he ended up on
			the moon of this new universe. He had doubts about whether people
			would accept him, so he created three extensions of himself to run a
			little experiment, which is how The Son, The Knight and The Queen
			were born. All three went somewhat insane, and Nixon concluded that
			he couldn't risk entering an unfriendly planet. Besides, he already
			knew that the Son would become King of the Lunarians, and that if he
			didn't stop it, he would become exceedingly powerful.
		</p>
		<center>
			<p>
				I am sorry, Mr Dwight. No human was ever meant to hear what I
				have said.
			</p>
		</center>
		<p>
			Back on our planet, the Queen of the Lunarians tries to talk to the
			Knight telepathically, trying to convince him to leave Earth and
			join the kingdom as Prince, to bring a place of harmony, to repair
			the peace equation, so that he can return to his old self. However,
			the Knight, amidst all the anger he has, still fulfils the words of
			Alice Avenue: “At all times, in all places, the Knight can SAVE US”,
			and unleashes a final attack that would not only destroy him, the
			Queen and the Lunarians, but also restore human culture within 9
			months: <b>ALCATRAZ CHECKMATE</b>.
		</p>
		<p>
			However, there is still the King, who has finally become aware of
			all he has done, and breaks down in tears once again. Grief made him
			a monster, he will not stop crying, he does not want to live, but in
			that instant, he mutates again, assimilating a very familiar form to
			the Knight's helmet, becoming what Nixon feared he would become... <b
				><u>THE HORNED SERPENT LIVES</u></b
			>.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<img
		src="../../../images/data/thehornedserpentlives_dark.png"
		class="logo toggleable"
	/>
	<Trans i18nKey="nixon.part7">
		<blockquote>
			<center><p><b><u>THE HORNED SERPENT LIVES</u></b></p></center>
		</blockquote>
		<p>
			Nixon must act fast, he can't let it all end like his own world
			ended, so he decided to render the King, the Knight, the Queen, and
			himself as fiction, so no one will believe in the Crescent King and
			so he loses his powers. That's how this whole world became a comic
			book called “The Nixonverse”, with an endearing story made by a
			certain “Mister Manticore” and beautiful illustrations made by... <b
				>Ed Dwight?</b
			>
		</p>
		<p>
			Compared to Nixon, Ed Dwight was twice the God he was, Nixon was
			just one of many survivors who erased the past, to run from the
			present. Ed was everything Nixon wasn't, someone bold, kind and
			good. He never went to the moon, let alone talked to a God, he is
			today in our world creating monuments... <i
				>Ed Dwight preserves the past.</i
			>
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<a
		href="https://twitter.com/MagicBunnyStar/status/1555336147139715076"
		target="_blank"
	>
		<img
			src="../../../images/data/preservethepast_dark.png"
			class="logo toggleable"
		/>
	</a>
</Layout>
